==================== CLAUDE ANALYSIS, CYCLE 3 (rounds 4-5) ====================
What happened: benchmark now 48 matchups x 6 seeds. Round 4 promoted c2 (layout_jitter 20->10, population 48->72);
round 5 kept the champion (c1, the orbit-focus child, scored +0.163 vs +0.154 but under the 0.01 bar).
The two rounds took 18.0 and 20.8 minutes: the population-72 tweak raised the cost (the same drift as the
overnight run), so the cycle ran about 39 minutes instead of 30.

Identical batch (60 unseen matchups x 4 seeds, analysis_cycle3.txt), overnight champion -> round 3 -> now:
  all:      60% -> 62% -> 64% win   (timeouts 20 -> 18 -> 16%, losses unchanged at 20%)
  power:    stronger 84 -> 87 -> 88%, close 64 -> 68 -> 70%, weaker 27 -> 28 -> 31%
  opponent: orbit 44 -> 46 -> 52% (timeouts 52 -> 49 -> 44%), hold 82 -> 87 -> 88%, charge 61 -> 62 -> 64%, kite 51 -> 53 -> 54%
  type:     brawl 46 -> 55%, line 63 -> 71%, scout 47 -> 49%, artillery 59 -> 61%, raid 82 -> 84%
  close vs orbit 49 -> 63%, stronger vs orbit 73 -> 81%.

What we learned:
 1. The climb is real but slow: +2 points over two rounds, and nearly all of it is against orbit (the council
    is learning to close on circling units), plus line and brawl platoons. Kite and scouts did not move.
 2. Against charge and kite the remaining losses are mostly physical: weaker side vs charge 22%, vs kite 12%.
    Stronger vs kite still loses 16% (a faster kiting platoon cannot be caught), unchanged by training.
 3. Cycle-by-cycle gain on a fixed batch: +8 (cycle 1, different batch), 0 (cycle 2), +2 (cycle 3). I read the win
    rate as close to asymptotic for this council and objective: the remaining headroom is in kite-chasing, which
    probably needs inputs the council does not have (speed advantage, turn rate).
 4. Selection pressure toward cost happened again, so population is now capped at 56.

What to change (applied for cycle 4): population cap 56 (incumbent reset to 48); everything else as cycle 3.
Decision rule for the objectives stage: if cycle 4 gains less than 1 point on the same batch, treat the win rate as
asymptotic and start the attack/defend objectives (scenario design in docs/OBJECTIVES_PLAN.md).
