==================== CLAUDE ANALYSIS, CYCLE 4 (rounds 6-7) ====================
What happened: population capped at 56, otherwise as cycle 3. Round 6 promoted c2 (l1 0.05->0.1, seeds_per_battle 2->4),
round 7 kept the champion. The rounds took 22.9 and 29.6 minutes: seeds_per_battle 4 and population 56 were adopted/tried and
cost 2x per child, so this cycle ran about 52 minutes. Selection sees score, not cost; I did not cap seeds_per_battle at 2.

Identical batch (analysis_cycle4.txt): round-4 champion 64% win -> current champion (round 6) 63%. Within noise, if anything
slightly worse: orbit 52 -> 49, kite 54 -> 51, charge 64 -> 62, hold 88 -> 91. By power: stronger 88 -> 87, close 70 -> 68,
weaker 31 -> 31. The round-6 promotion was noise again, even with a 48-matchup benchmark.

Conclusion: the win rate is asymptotic for this council, objective and roster: +8, 0, +2, -1 points over four cycles
on fixed batches. The decision rule from cycle 3 (< 1 point gain => start objectives) is met. Reference champion for the
next stage is the ROUND-4 champion (hall_of_fame/champion-r0004.json, 64%), not the round-6 one.

What we learned overall: (1) generated platoon matchups gave a large early gain in generalisation (cycle 1) and then a
plateau; (2) the remaining losses are mostly physical (weaker side vs charge/kite) or chase problems (stronger vs kite, 16%
losses) that the council cannot learn without speed/turn-rate inputs; (3) round-to-round scores cannot be trusted below about
0.05, so promotions should be judged on a fixed batch, which analyze_matchups.py does; (4) the loop's cost drifts upward
whenever a bigger setting is tried, so any knob that raises cost needs a hard cap.

What to change: stop the plain platoon-matchup loop here and begin the objectives stage (docs/OBJECTIVES_PLAN.md): engine
objective ending, attack/defend baseline with the round-4 champion, then tactical_v4 inputs. Possible later retest of the plain
loop after v4 adds speed-advantage / turn-rate inputs, which is the main remaining hypothesis for kite/scout weakness.

==================== CLAUDE: STAGE CHANGE ====================
The plain platoon loop is stopped (asymptote reached, see cycle 4). Objectives work continues in data/brains/obj/ (its own
evolve.log): engine-side outcome rules for attack/defend, a target structure behind its owner's platoons, objective-aware
baselines `strike` and `guard`, and a baseline of the round-4 champion (data/brains/obj/baseline_v3.txt).
Baseline of the unchanged council on objective fights: attack 67% win (vs guard 82% with 18% timeouts, vs charge 51%, kite 47%),
defend 79% win (vs strike 77%, charge 60%, kite 64%, orbit 74%). Plain fights in the same batch: 66%.
